  "verbalization": "Tectoruside appears to have a shared target relationship with NCI-H446 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the regulation of cellular processes. The evidence suggests that Tectoruside acts on VMRC-LCP, which is a target of Glycitein and 7-Angeloylechinatine, and ultimately leads to NCI-H446. This indicates a potential pathway where Tectoruside may influence NCI-H446 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly by modulating the activity of these intermediates. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The presence of multiple targets implies that Tectoruside may exert its effects through a complex network of molecular interactions, potentially involving multiple pathways or cellular processes.",
